@startuml seller-receiving-money-flow
!define STRIPE_COLOR #FFE082
!define BACKEND_COLOR #E1F5FF
!define BANK_COLOR #C8E6C9

start
:Buyer completes payment;
:Money enters Stripe\nplatform account;

:Stripe deducts\nplatform fee (10%);

:Calculate seller earnings\n(90% of transaction);

:Seller earnings recorded\nin payout_ledger;

if (Seller Stripe Connect\naccount ready?) then (No)
  :Hold funds as\nPENDING balance;
  :Wait for seller to\ncomplete onboarding;
  :Once seller verified → ACTIVE;
else (Yes)
  :Skip waiting;
endif

:Move funds to seller\nConnected account\n(on Stripe);

:Check payout schedule\n(based on seller settings);

:Apply payout schedule:
  - Instant: within minutes
  - Daily: daily cycle
  - Weekly: weekly cycle
  - Monthly: monthly cycle;

:Stripe sends funds\nto seller bank account;

:Update payout_ledger\nstatus = PAID;

:Seller sees bank deposit;

:Seller balance updated\nto AVAILABLE;

stop

note right
  Key Points:
  - Stripe owns the transfer rails
  - Your app just tracks accounting
  - Bank deposits happen on Stripe's schedule
  - Database reflects the source of truth
  - Webhooks confirm all state changes
end note

@enduml
